Done. Two files created:

**`fetchall.go`** — bounded-concurrency processor using:
- Buffered channel as semaphore (at most `concurrency` in flight)
- `sync.WaitGroup.Go()` (Go 1.25+) for safe goroutine lifecycle
- `errors.Join()` for aggregate error where `errors.Is`/`errors.As` reach every individual failure
- `sort.Slice` to order results by `Index`

**`fetchall_test.go`** — 11 tests covering:
- Basic success with result ordering
- Empty inputs → `(nil, nil)`
- Invalid concurrency (< 1) → error
- Concurrency limit enforcement (verified with atomic counter)
- Error aggregation: mixed success/failure, `errors.Is`/`errors.As` reachable
- All-fail case
- Context cancellation (mid-flight and pre-cancelled)
- Concurrency > len(inputs) (all run in parallel)
- Partial cancellation (fast results collected before cancellation)

All gates pass: `go build`, `go vet`, `go test`, and `rulecheck` (via `check.sh`).
